# Same molecule/basis as water.inp, pushed further toward the
# nonrelativistic limit (c -> infinity) than water-c1000.inp. The
# "positive energy" eigenvalues should be nearly indistinguishable from
# water-c1000.inp's now. This is also roughly where floating-point
# rounding starts to show up in the Kramers-pair splitting check (the
# eigenvalues' magnitude, ~-2c^2, has grown large enough that double
# precision's ~16 significant digits can no longer fully resolve a tiny
# splitting riding on top of it) -- an inherent numerical limitation of
# testing literal c -> infinity this way, not a sign of a bug.
SPEED_OF_LIGHT = 100000
NELEC 10
BASIS water-sto-3g.gbs

GEOMETRY
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.757000   0.586000
H   0.000000  -0.757000   0.586000
END
